- I am also frustrated *with* the way “maximizing efficiency” has somehow been elevated to the paramount value in many conversations. Learning is messy and, as [Josh Brake](https://open.substack.com/users/21090761-josh-brake?utm_source=mentions) noted recently, [“There is no salvation to be found in efficiency.”](https://substack.com/redirect/211aa7cc-9f22-49c5-965f-6d476263d6b5?j=eyJ1IjoiNGVqN2FuIn0.oGvUXgUaORh_ZN3LcglypAdZpT_HSJ5iro3JlPLHSFk) Nevertheless, the proliferation of AI in pursuit of increased productivity has come to feel like our 21st-century Gold Rush in education, metaphorically and, at times, [quite literally](https://substack.com/redirect/96afa158-2aab-4b6d-b096-2f9a2aaf4efa?j=eyJ1IjoiNGVqN2FuIn0.oGvUXgUaORh_ZN3LcglypAdZpT_HSJ5iro3JlPLHSFk). ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01jvj12ngj5jr5eszryxzsqt2h))
